<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Ottoman Tunisia</h1><p class="st-meta">1574 CE – 1705 CE · capital Tunis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tunis as an Ottoman province, where power shifted from pashas to Janissary deys and then to the hereditary Muradid beys.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1574 an Ottoman expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koca-sinan-pasha">Sinan Pasha</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-goulette">La Goulette</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsid</a> client, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hafsid-sultanate">Hafsid Sultanate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> became a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under a pasha, with a strong <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> garrison.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> revolt in 1591 put power in the hands of deys, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uthman-dey">Uthman Dey</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-dey">Yusuf Dey</a>, who welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> after 1609; they founded towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/testour">Testour</a>. Corsairing and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> trade brought wealth. Meanwhile the beys, commanders of the tax-collecting army, grew stronger, and Murad Bey's descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muradid-dynasty">Muradids</a>, became hereditary rulers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammuda-pasha-bey">Hammuda Pasha Bey</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muradid-dynasty">Muradid</a> succession wars from 1675 and invasions from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a> weakened the state. In 1702 the Muradid line was destroyed, and in 1705 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a> seized power, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beylik-of-tunis">Husainid dynasty</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ottoman-tunisia.jpg" alt="Ottoman Tunisia" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Rayan54 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ottoman_Tunisia_(1685).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1574 CE – 1705 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tunis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Uthman Dey, Yusuf Dey, Hammuda Pasha Bey</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Ottoman Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regency of Tunis (Muradid), Eyalet of Tunis, Muradid beylik</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1640&amp;focus=ottoman-tunisia" aria-label="Ottoman Tunisia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4935 851 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ottoman Tunisia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5255 1107L5255 1107M5255 1107L5709 970M5255 1107L5255 1107"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5255 1107h0M5709 970h0M5255 1107h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5255 1107h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5255 1107h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tunis. <a href="/atlas?year=1640&amp;focus=ottoman-tunisia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
